#
#   The board-support package for the ESP32-P4 bring-up.
#
#   This is the standard AROS PKG v1 container, not a linked image.  Its
#   members are complete relocatable module files; the platform ELF loader
#   places and relocates them in PSRAM later.
#
#   A4 grew the package in measured steps: first the DOS side, then the
#   emergency console, each proven to load, relocate and initialise while the
#   post-krnStartExec() diagnostics could still be read.  `dosboot.resource`
#   is the last of them, and the reason for that order: its COLDSTART init
#   either boots or retries for ever, so from here on nothing after
#   `krnStartExec()` in kernel_startup.c is reachable.  What replaces those
#   diagnostics is the modules' own narration, which needs DOS_DEBUG=1 and
#   DOSBOOT_DEBUG=1 to exist at all, and the heartbeat task the kickstart
#   starts from a COLDSTART resident at -40.
#
#   Note that `econsole` and `sdcard.device`'s `SDCard boot wait` resident
#   share priority -49.  That tie is harmless: one registers a boot node at
#   bootpri -127 and the other waits for pending bus tasks, neither depends
#   on the other, and dosboot at -50 follows both whichever way the link
#   order falls.  A resident that does depend on the order would have to say
#   so with a distinct priority rather than rely on this.
#

include $(SRCDIR)/config/aros.cfg
include $(SRCDIR)/arch/riscv-esp32p4/board/board.mk

